# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Music ignore list (EXAMPLE / REFERENCE FILE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `ignored/music.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix) and
# uncomment / edit entries below as needed. The real `music.yaml` is
# gitignored so personal library decisions don't leak into the repo.
#
# Each entry is a path prefix. Any music-pass warning whose `path` field
# starts with one of these (followed by `/` or end-of-string,
# case-insensitive, separator-normalized) gets silently dropped from
# `output/music/warnings.json` (and counted in the run summary).
#
# Get paths from `output/music/warnings.json`. Most music warnings use the
# `<Artist>/<Album>` path shape.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Silence a whole artist ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Useful when an artist's whole catalog has a known issue you've decided
# to keep (e.g. a folder/tag mismatch you can't fix because the tag is set
# by the original publisher).
# - Some Artist
# - Various Artists

# ── Silence one album ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drops every warning under this album folder (compilation_detected,
# folder_tag_mismatch, missing_tags, track_number_mismatch, etc.).
# - Pink Floyd/The Wall
# - 2Pac/All Eyez on Me

# ── Silence a single track ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin-point: just one file path.
# - Pink Floyd/The Wall/01 - In the Flesh.flac

# ── Silence by category ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drop ALL warnings under a category folder.
# - Other Music
# - Other Soundtracks
